54619 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754619 1077 "response" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754619 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754634 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754619 1079 #uuid "7257176f-4481-583c-91f6-109a9f35061d" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754620 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754813 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754620 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754620 1077 "answer" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754620 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754813 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754620 1079 #uuid "7393ac36-306c-5308-942a-0da2a462f514" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754621 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754517 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754621 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754621 1077 "answer" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754621 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754517 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754621 1079 #uuid "73ee4a73-0349-5c59-87ab-fe5165823764" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754622 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754568 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754622 1071 "Source question: Assignment item (4); Kuttler 2017A, Exercise 4.10.44, printed p. 228 (PDF p. 240).\n\nFor a fixed $w\\in\\mathbb R^4$, let $M=\\{u\\in\\mathbb R^4:w\\cdot u=0\\}$. Is $M$ a subspace? Explain." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754622 1072 #uuid "74895bb8-28f7-53cc-b2c2-5f2d75753ac1" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754622 1074 "Use the subspace test and the dot product’s linearity; do not assume $w$ is nonzero." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754623 1062 #uuid "74f940a5-49a9-5cb3-9225-26df8b806151" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754623 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754554 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754624 1058 #edb/ref 17592186754636 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754624 1062 #uuid "757d8dc8-5e55-5725-a9bb-01da88d5beba" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754624 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754452 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754625 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754595 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754625 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754625 1077 "response" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754625 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754595 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754625 1079 #uuid "75baf3f7-b5cb-565e-9402-d3fa0791fb12" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754626 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048218 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754626 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048445 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754626 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049222 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754626 1088 #edb/ref 17592186051046 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754626 1089 #edb/ref 17592186754460 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754626 1090 #uuid "76231dc7-bafb-5fc8-bd82-c84bdbcd8365" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754627 1080 "3" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754627 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754627 1083 #uuid "76ab5ccf-37cb-5a67-a857-455e725a3a25" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754628 1084 #edb/ref 17592186754463 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754628 1084 #edb/ref 17592186754489 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754628 1084 #edb/ref 17592186754765 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754628 1084 #edb/ref 17592186754805 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754628 1085 "Source question: PDF p. 5, Problem 4 (a)–(d).\n\n**Laplacian.** On $[-\\pi,\\pi]\\times[-\\pi,\\pi]$, consider $f(x,y)=\\sin x+\\sin y$ and $\\nabla f=\\langle\\cos x,\\cos y\\rangle$. The Laplacian is $\\nabla^2f=\\nabla\\cdot(\\nabla f)$.\n\n![Source surface and gradient plot with blue minimum and red maximum](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FWHW-6%2Flaplacian-surface-and-gradient.png)" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754628 1086 #uuid "76d100bf-71c6-58a1-a753-66c046cb7de7" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754628 1087 #edb/ref 17592186754463 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754629 1080 "Symmetry gives $x^*=y^*=0$. Using $z=\\rho\\cos\\phi$ and $dV=\\rho^2\\sin\\phi\\,d\\rho\\,d\\phi\\,d\\theta$, take $0\\le\\rho\\le a$, $0\\le\\phi\\le\\pi/2$, $0\\le\\theta\\le2\\pi$. Then $$V=\\frac{2\\pi a^3}{3},\\qquad \\iiint_D z\\,dV=\\left(\\frac{a^4}{4}\\right)\\left(\\frac12\\right)(2\\pi)=\\frac{\\pi a^4}{4}.$$ Therefore $z^*=(\\pi a^4/4)/(2\\pi a^3/3)=3a/8$." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754629 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754629 1083 #uuid "7793a6db-9bde-539c-bf14-e336ef825c96" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754630 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754539 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754630 1071 "**(a)** Compute the Wronskian of $y_1=x^{r_1}$ and $y_2=x^{r_2}$ on $0<x<\\infty$.\n\n$W(x)=$ {{answer}}." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754630 1072 #uuid "783f6381-0780-5779-b665-328be19d11e2" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754630 1074 "The derivatives are $r_1x^{r_1-1}$ and $r_2x^{r_2-1}$. Hence $W=x^{r_1}r_2x^{r_2-1}-r_1x^{r_1-1}x^{r_2}=(r_2-r_1)x^{r_1+r_2-1}$, well-defined for $x>0$." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754631 1080 "\\frac{-1-\\sqrt{1-4m}}{2m}" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754631 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754631 1083 #uuid "78c04815-6538-5b23-b5e3-b2421ad7b5ee" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754632 1058 #edb/ref 17592186754740 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754632 1062 #uuid "794b48d5-f51b-5464-b0a8-0f89b770aa52" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754632 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754541 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754633 1062 #uuid "7a06ed11-3c56-5dd1-877d-2c5a22c4a203" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754633 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754437 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754634 1080 "No. Put them in a $5\\times6$ matrix $A$. It has at most five pivots, so the homogeneous system $Ax=0$ has at least one free variable and therefore a nonzero solution. This gives a nontrivial linear relation among the six vectors. An independent set in a five-dimensional space has at most five vectors." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754634 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754634 1083 #uuid "7a3d1417-a30f-5dc3-88a2-3494b4cc6b58" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754635 1058 #edb/ref 17592186754787 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754635 1062 #uuid "7ad2ceb6-fbe6-56dd-98bd-d4c42475b388" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754635 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754725 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754636 1058 #edb/ref 17592186754784 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754636 1062 #uuid "7af25f32-dd51-5513-9056-aa20292c687c" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754636 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754790 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754637 1084 #edb/ref 17592186754486 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754637 1084 #edb/ref 17592186754574 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754637 1085 "Source question: PDF p. 6, Problem 5 (a), bonus (b).\n\nFor single-variable differentiable scalar functions, $f\\prime=g\\prime$ on $(a,b)$ implies $f=g+c$, by applying the mean value theorem to $h=f-g$. Investigate the two proposed multivariable extensions below." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754637 1086 #uuid "7affa280-a9dc-58cc-9bea-6283be6e15d8" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754637 1087 #edb/ref 17592186754486 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754638 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754762 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754638 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754638 1077 "answer" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754638 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754762 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754638 1079 #uuid "7b13ada3-236c-512d-8312-78dc729a1710" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754639 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754606 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754639 1071 "**(a)** Show that $\\left(0,0,\\frac{3a}{8}\\right)$ is the centroid of the solid hemisphere $x^2+y^2+z^2\\le a^2$, $z\\ge0$, with $a>0$." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754639 1072 #uuid "7b4e61d7-de6c-5052-b239-48cf3a348be8" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754639 1074 "Compute the solid-volume moment, rather than a surface-area moment. The supplied formula is for a filled hemisphere." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754640 1084 #edb/ref 17592186754470 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754640 1084 #edb/ref 17592186754643 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754640 1084 #edb/ref 17592186754755 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754640 1084 #edb/ref 17592186754776 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754640 1085 "Source question: PDF p. 1, Problem 1 (a)–(d).\n\nSuppose $y_1(x)=e^{r_1x}$ and $y_2(x)=e^{r_2x}$ solve $ay\\prime\\prime+by\\prime+cy=0$." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754640 1086 #uuid "7b8d994c-ed01-5865-9d41-440ce1e1e347" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754640 1087 #edb/ref 17592186754470 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754641 1062 #uuid "7bc7ff7a-d183-5b77-9ff7-b7515e63ce06" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754641 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754771 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754642 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050537 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754642 1089 #edb/ref 17592186754690 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754642 1090 #uuid "7c372fbf-b75e-5448-873a-46517898f975" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754643 1062 #uuid "7c9bda1d-f013-574f-abe2-6054b931798d" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754643 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754515 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754644 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754479 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754644 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754644 1077 "response" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754644 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754479 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754644 1079 #uuid "7e4efe93-bf14-5395-9678-dc79dc6b533d" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754645 1058 #edb/ref 17592186754612 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754645 1062 #uuid "7f393222-4d21-5003-9655-6747efa62a6c" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754645 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754699 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754646 1080 "Yes. The substituted trial gives $A_0+2A_1+(2A_1+6A_2)x+3A_2x^2$. Matching with $1+2x+x^2$ yields $3A_2=1$, $2A_1+6A_2=2$, and $A_0+2A_1=1$. Thus $A_2=1/3$, $A_1=0$, $A_0=1$, so $y_p=x+x^3/3$. Its derivatives are $1+x^2$ and $2x$, whose sum is the forcing." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754646 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754646 1083 #uuid "7f7f129b-ee5b-57e2-8fcb-954714d5c24c" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754647 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048781 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754647 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049459 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754647 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049676 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754647 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050143 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754647 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050172 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754647 1088 #edb/ref 17592186051048 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754647 1089 #edb/ref 17592186754628 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754647 1090 #uuid "7fcba558-d3b8-56c1-8175-2bd34c2d3092" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754648 1080 "(c_1+c_2t)e^{-2t}" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754648 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754648 1083 #uuid "7fd5f02d-5848-59f8-b7da-d00f533a910b" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754649 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754442 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754649 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754669 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754649 1071 "**(d)** Calculate $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F$ and compare its components with your answers in (a)–(c).\n\n$\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=$ {{curl}}. Give the comparison in the written-response field." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754649 1072 #uuid "817ef473-efe6-5c8b-8e78-23933fcf2667" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754649 1074 "Compute $(R_y-Q_z,P_z-R_x,Q_x-P_y)$ for $(P,Q,R)=(0,z,0)$ and apply the right-hand rule." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754650 1080 "\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\0\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754650 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754650 1083 #uuid "81b9522b-69ac-5b7d-aac6-76e58800322f" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754651 1088 #edb/ref 17592186051085 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754651 1089 #edb/ref 17592186754738 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754651 1090 #uuid "81beeb68-8878-5356-a69b-775a2f4529df" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754652 1084 #edb/ref 17592186754499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754652 1084 #edb/ref 17592186754701 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754652 1084 #edb/ref 17592186754744 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754652 1085 "Source question: PDF p. 2, Problem 2 (a)–(c).\n\nSuppose $y_1(x)=x^{r_1}$ and $y_2(x)=x^{r_2}$ solve $ax^2y\\prime\\prime+bxy\\prime+cy=0$." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754652 1086 #uuid "83aa3899-bf97-5c1a-bed2-e8f173679746" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754652 1087 #edb/ref 17592186754701 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754653 1062 #uuid "83d31e32-1928-5fc2-8b52-a25178b0b58a" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754653 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754559 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754654 1062 #uuid "8564167f-db1c-5242-aeae-78f14a674ad9" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754654 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754582 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754655 1080 "The scaling $x=au,y=bv,z=cw$ maps the upper unit half-ball $D_0$ to the semi-ellipsoid and has $dV=abc\\,du\\,dv\\,dw$. Its volume is $abc(2\\pi/3)$, and its $z$-moment is $abc^2(\\pi/4)$. Symmetry gives the first two centroid coordinates zero, and $$z^*=\\frac{abc^2\\pi/4}{abc\\,2\\pi/3}=\\frac{3c}{8}.$$ The scale factors $a,b$ cancel." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754655 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754655 1083 #uuid "85bb859d-6ae8-5abd-9aee-f1cebb321da8" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754656 1080 "2" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754656 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754656 1083 #uuid "87543245-2b09-55c1-b164-ea0446b53432" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754657 1080 "At each point $(0,0,z)$ draw $\\mathbf E=\\sin z\\,\\mathbf i$ along the $x$-direction and $\\mathbf B=\\sin z\\,\\mathbf j$ along the $y$-direction. The two arrows have the same signed amplitude, are perpendicular, and reverse together at $z=\\pi$. They both vanish at $0,\\pi,2\\pi$.\n\n![Authored reference: simultaneous electric and magnetic vectors](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FWHW-6%2Fauthored-maxwell-combined.png)" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754657 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754657 1083 #uuid "8761d4b0-fad6-5198-a363-6857c3fdfc63" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754658 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754564 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754658 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754658 1077 "response" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754658 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754564 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754658 1079 #uuid "87c8f7da-7a90-51ea-9e52-7b1f687a4dcd" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754659 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754830 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754659 1071 "**(a)** The wheel axis points in the $\\mathbf i$ direction: it rotates freely in a plane parallel to the $yz$-plane, viewed from the positive $x$-axis. From the source plot, does it rotate? Enter **CW**, **CCW**, or **no rotation**.\n\nResponse: {{answer}}." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754659 1072 #uuid "880011e9-2027-564d-b2bd-6d0ec43567f4" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754659 1074 "The $x$-component of curl is $\\partial_yF_z-\\partial_zF_y=0-1=-1$. A negative rotation component gives clockwise motion when viewed from the positive $x$-axis." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754660 1058 #edb/ref 17592186754594 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754660 1062 #uuid "88353905-f399-58df-978b-c0306c6a6705" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754660 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754783 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754661 1080 "3" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754661 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754661 1083 #uuid "88558422-e78f-59ca-adeb-99a74012fb8f" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754662 1062 #uuid "88604773-904c-5c66-9392-aa898ee7c462" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754662 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754613 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754663 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754533 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754663 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754791 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754663 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754796 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754663 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754838 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754663 1071 "**(b)** Find the local minimum (blue) and local maximum (red), and evaluate the Laplacian at each. Give positions on the surface as column vectors $(x,y,z)^T$.\n\nMinimum position: {{minimum}}. Laplacian there: {{lap-min}}.\n\nMaximum position: {{maximum}}. Laplacian there: {{lap-max}}." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754663 1072 #uuid "895963b0-6b43-5ae5-8858-57191e0515d3" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754663 1074 "Critical points satisfy $\\cos x=\\cos y=0$. At $(-\\pi/2,-\\pi/2)$ the Hessian is the identity, so the surface has a local minimum $z=-2$ and Laplacian $2$. At $(\\pi/2,\\pi/2)$ the Hessian is minus the identity, giving a local maximum $z=2$ and Laplacian $-2$. The other two critical points are saddles." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754664 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754523 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754664 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754576 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754664 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754832 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754664 1071 "**(b)** $\\mathbf F=\\langle x,y^2\\rangle$.\n\n![Source plot for divergence predictions](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-6%2Fdivergence-field-b.png)\n\nFirst write your two predicted signs and visual reasoning in the written-response field. Then compute:\n\n$\\operatorname{div}\\mathbf F(1,1)=$ {{div-one}}; $\\operatorname{div}\\mathbf F(1,-2)=$ {{div-two}}." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754664 1072 #uuid "8a1b7e63-99fe-57d7-9db6-22daffa93b6e" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754664 1074 "Observe how neighboring vectors differ, rather than using the sign of the vertical velocity itself; divergence measures the derivative $2y$." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754665 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754474 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754665 1071 "**(j)** $\\nabla\\cdot(\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F)$.\n\nClassification: {{answer}}." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754665 1072 #uuid "8b0c6439-15b5-56ea-8ae9-4b0a2704e238" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754665 1074 "The inner divergence is scalar, so it cannot be the input to another divergence." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754666 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048218 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754666 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049340 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754666 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050426 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754666 1089 #edb/ref 17592186754449 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754666 1090 #uuid "8b521e07-684e-54c1-97d2-0b220a9644d5" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754667 1058 #edb/ref 17592186754733 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754667 1062 #uuid "8c14b4e6-c688-5f0d-828a-759c1b52d028" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754667 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754800 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754668 1080 "scalar function" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754668 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754668 1083 #uuid "8d8b5dca-adb5-5a10-83a4-68a2d55ef97b" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754669 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754650 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754669 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754669 1077 "curl" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754669 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754650 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754669 1079 #uuid "8d9abef7-d4e9-5725-94a8-958d66a78342" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754670 1080 "\\frac{-1+\\sqrt{1-4m}}{2m}" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754670 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754670 1083 #uuid "8e4f26bb-d3c4-5fc1-9106-782ddc7a8c6d" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754671 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754763 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754671 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754671 1077 "answer" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754671 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754763 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754671 1079 #uuid "8e58e470-59ef-5d9b-99ef-1dd6b52606ab" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754672 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754692 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754672 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754672 1077 "response" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754672 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754692 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754672 1079 #uuid "900dee7c-8cd0-5b4a-a28b-4b67bb6d22d9" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754673 1088 #edb/ref 17592186048445 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754673 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049009 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754673 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049222 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754673 1088 #edb/ref 17592186050028 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754673 1089 #edb/ref 17592186754599 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754673 1090 #uuid "900f895b-05b3-5b91-92f1-7a3a2a511e4f" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754674 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754575 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754674 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754674 1077 "response" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754674 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754575 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754674 1079 #uuid "904b4dd9-3b46-531f-89b8-ce2d90eaa62f" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754802 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754675 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754675 1077 "answer" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754675 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754802 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754675 1079 #uuid "93050dde-73d1-5918-8f84-ebca6c42775e" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754676 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754713 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754676 1071 "Source question: PDF p. 5, Problem 4.\n\nEvaluate $\\displaystyle\\iiint_Dxy\\,dV$, where $D$ is bounded by $x-y=0$, $x-y=2$, $z-x=0$, $z-x=1$, $z=0$, and $z=2$. Show transformed bounds and supporting work.\n\nIntegral $=$ {{answer}}." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754676 1072 #uuid "9343e082-7e62-5713-aa85-216bfd310fd5" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754676 1074 "Choose $u=x-y$, $v=z-x$, $w=z$. Then $x=w-v$, $y=w-v-u$, $z=w$, and the absolute Jacobian is $1$. The box is $0\\le u\\le2$, $0\\le v\\le1$, $0\\le w\\le2$. Thus $$I=\\int_0^2\\int_0^1\\int_0^2(w-v)(w-v-u)\\,du\\,dv\\,dw.$$ The $u$-integral is $2(w-v)^2-2(w-v)$; the $v$-integral is $2w^2-4w+5/3$. Integrating from $0$ to $2$ gives $2/3$." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754677 1080 "vector field" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754677 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754677 1083 #uuid "94125714-4c33-5ab8-aa24-a4f9353a46e7" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754678 1080 "2" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754678 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754678 1083 #uuid "943b4e36-3290-547c-bf0c-0aa15421c8c6" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754679 1058 #edb/ref 17592186754615 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754679 1062 #uuid "945cb466-caca-568b-87f5-efa1ecc01b34" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754679 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754720 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754680 1080 "The change $x=au,y=bv$ sends the unit upper semicircle $D$ to the semiellipse, with $dA=ab\\,du\\,dv$. Thus $A=ab(\\pi/2)$ and $$\\iint_Ry\\,dA=ab^2\\iint_Dv\\,du\\,dv=ab^2\\frac23.$$ Symmetry gives $x^*=0$ and the ratio gives $y^*=4b/(3\\pi)$. The horizontal scale $a$ cancels." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754680 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754680 1083 #uuid "947bce18-bb5c-50cd-b34b-a2b3d40efeec" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754681 1062 #uuid "94a53db5-d430-5a3b-81bb-cdee07000023" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754681 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754482 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754682 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754447 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754682 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754682 1077 "response" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754682 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754447 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754682 1079 #uuid "94bbefdb-207a-5928-bea7-353a39413c02" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754683 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754715 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754683 1071 "Source question: Assignment item (1); Kuttler 2017A, Exercise 4.10.21, printed p. 224 (PDF p. 236).\n\nThe following five vectors lie in $\\mathbb R^4$, in the listed order $v_1,\\ldots,v_5$: $$\\left\\{\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\\\-1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix},\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\2\\\\-1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix},\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\-2\\\\-1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix},\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\2\\\\0\\\\1\\end{pmatrix},\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\-1\\\\-1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}\\right\\}.$$ Explain why they cannot be linearly independent. Then find a linearly independent subset with the same span, that is, a basis for their span." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754683 1072 #uuid "94e7f99e-2b22-52fb-8b46-7b923c3d4db4" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754683 1074 "Use the number of vectors versus the ambient dimension for the first claim. To extract a basis, choose pivot columns from the original matrix, not the reduced matrix." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754684 1080 "vector field" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754684 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754684 1083 #uuid "95cd7723-3dc1-5d43-a43c-c0308b83b2a0" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754685 1043 #edb/ref 17592186754542 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754685 1043 #edb/ref 17592186754614 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754685 1043 #edb/ref 17592186754615 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754685 1043 #edb/ref 17592186754653 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754685 1043 #edb/ref 17592186754679 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754685 1043 #edb/ref 17592186754812 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754685 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045461 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754685 1045 "MTH 255 — WHW-6" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754685 1046 #edb/ref 17592186754812 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754685 1047 #inst "2026-11-06T07:59:00.000Z" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754685 1048 #edb/ref 17592186405204 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754685 1053 #uuid "9631ca08-4da9-51d3-8388-9ace90604bfd" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754686 1088 #edb/ref 17592186051085 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754686 1089 #edb/ref 17592186754577 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754686 1090 #uuid "96d9b2bc-eb74-5a36-a164-6bcdf44ad4d5" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754648 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754687 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754687 1077 "answer" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754687 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754648 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754687 1079 #uuid "9719a65b-a098-57da-bd74-becdc8d24d21" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754688 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754521 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754688 1071 "**(b)(i)** Take $a=k=1$ and $t=0$. Draw $\\mathbf E(z)$ and $\\mathbf B(z)$ separately for $0\\le z\\le2\\pi$. For every chosen $z$, draw a vertical vector with tail at $(z,0)$.\n\n![Source axes for separate electric and magnetic field sketches](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FWHW-6%2Fmaxwell-separate-axes.png)" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754688 1072 #uuid "974a1e75-967a-5eb9-befe-ea685d10ac77" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754688 1074 "Use arrows whose signed heights follow $\\sin z$, with every tail on the $z$-axis; label which component belongs to each field." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754689 1058 #edb/ref 17592186754779 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754689 1062 #uuid "9769fc45-5ed6-563e-892b-783ebabbd0d4" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754689 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754593 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754690 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754476 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754690 1071 "Source question: PDF p. 5, Problem 4.\n\nOn $(a,b)$ suppose $y_{p1}\\prime\\prime+p(x)y_{p1}\\prime+q(x)y_{p1}=f_1(x)$ and $y_{p2}\\prime\\prime+p(x)y_{p2}\\prime+q(x)y_{p2}=f_2(x)$. Show that $y_p=y_{p1}+y_{p2}$ solves $$y\\prime\\prime+p(x)y\\prime+q(x)y=f_1(x)+f_2(x).$$" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754690 1072 #uuid "9a9a4e05-7858-554b-8474-66dadc4566ed" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754690 1074 "Expand the operator on the sum and group all terms belonging to each original particular solution. The coefficient functions stay the same for both equations." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754691 1058 #edb/ref 17592186754645 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754691 1062 #uuid "9ab9ec59-af0f-51c8-8614-129913e574e1" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754691 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754839 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754692 1080 "The assertion is false. On $\\mathbb R^3$, take $\\mathbf F=\\langle x,-y,0\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf G=\\mathbf0$. Then $\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F=1-1+0=0=\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf G$ and $\\nabla\\times\\mathbf F=\\mathbf0=\\nabla\\times\\mathbf G$, but $\\mathbf F-\\mathbf G=\\langle x,-y,0\\rangle$ is not constant. Thus matching curl and divergence do not determine a vector field up to a constant." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754692 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754692 1083 #uuid "9cb45e59-736f-5531-bbef-4aaa688072b1" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754693 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754826 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754693 1071 "**(e)** $\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F$.\n\nClassification: {{answer}}." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754693 1072 #uuid "9d6e4ba6-a55c-5c09-8c64-b8ad263c52e6" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754693 1074 "Divergence sums component derivatives and produces a scalar function." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754694 1062 #uuid "9ddc20c4-ee0e-5d4e-9313-ffb9397ac4b6" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754694 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754611 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754695 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754703 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754695 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754695 1077 "response" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754695 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754703 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754695 1079 #uuid "9dea5322-e84a-5fd8-a0ee-42bc75820f5d" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754696 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754723 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754696 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754696 1077 "answer" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754696 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754723 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754696 1079 #uuid "a14bc405-14d4-5d7c-b7fd-922cb51ee59b" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754697 1080 "Yes. Form the $5\\times5$ matrix $A$ with those vectors as columns. Independence means $Ax=0$ has only the zero solution, so every one of the five columns is a pivot column. There are therefore five pivot rows as well. For every $b\\in\\mathbb R^5$, the equation $Ax=b$ has a solution, so the columns span $\\mathbb R^5$. Equivalently, an independent set with exactly the dimension of the ambient space is a basis." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754697 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754697 1083 #uuid "a297fc03-f693-5aa5-952d-285d6bd2bd35" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754698 1068 #edb/ref 17592186754823 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754698 1071 "**(a)** Find the heat-flow field $\\mathbf F=-k\\nabla T$ and draw it throughout the interior of the ball." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754698 1072 #uuid "a2dc9e94-be6b-50c9-b44c-a39321f34092" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754698 1074 "Differentiate the temperature and apply the minus sign in Fourier’s law. The field points toward lower temperature." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754699 1088 #edb/ref 17592186049459 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754699 1089 #edb/ref 17592186754537 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754699 1090 #uuid "a2ecc92a-f2bb-5152-8c07-b5a3be054ea1" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754700 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754670 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754700 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754700 1077 "root-plus" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754700 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754670 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754700 1079 #uuid "a3017e5e-f635-537f-8a19-0c800bd80031" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754701 1058 #edb/ref 17592186754744 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754701 1062 #uuid "a31b895c-bb63-5e39-b3a7-bf4586d23ed5" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754701 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754630 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754702 1062 #uuid "a37636e6-433f-5e73-b038-a9d2ad63c9ae" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754702 1063 #edb/ref 17592186754664 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754703 1080 "Yes. On $x>0$, the factor $x^{r_1+r_2-1}$ is nonzero. Since $r_2-r_1\\ne0$, the Wronskian never vanishes. The normalized Cauchy–Euler coefficients are continuous on this interval, and the two functions are assumed to solve the ODE, so they are a fundamental set." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754703 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754703 1083 #uuid "a40481ff-0653-576c-a3d0-888491703541" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754704 1080 "3" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754704 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754704 1083 #uuid "a4095f76-28ca-5163-b2cf-1c9254ca7741" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754705 1080 "Both component profiles equal $\\sin z$. Vectors point in the positive component direction on $(0,\\pi)$, in the negative direction on $(\\pi,2\\pi)$, and have zero length at $0,\\pi,2\\pi$. Their maximum lengths are $1$ at $z=\\pi/2,3\\pi/2$. In the first plot the component axis is $x$; in the second it is $y$.\n\n![Authored reference: separate sine-profile vector sketches](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FWHW-6%2Fauthored-maxwell-separate.png)" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754705 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754705 1083 #uuid "a41e29c8-f65b-5c82-97c6-028236aa609c" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754706 1080 "Predict positive divergence at $(1,1)$ and negative divergence at $(1,-2)$. The horizontal contribution is $1$ everywhere; the vertical contribution is $2y$. Thus $\\nabla\\cdot\\mathbf F=1+2y$, giving $3$ at $(1,1)$ and $-3$ at $(1,-2)$. Below the axis, upward flow decreases in magnitude as $y$ increases, producing net compression." 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754706 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754706 1083 #uuid "a5630a02-5b81-58d6-891c-001d423ccd60" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754707 1075 #edb/ref 17592186754646 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754707 1076 #edb/ref 17592186408167 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754707 1077 "response" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754707 1078 #edb/ref 17592186754646 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754707 1079 #uuid "a5d3a31e-8a79-527f-93fd-a7a1633ef416" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754708 1043 #edb/ref 17592186754448 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754708 1043 #edb/ref 17592186754507 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754708 1043 #edb/ref 17592186754612 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754708 1043 #edb/ref 17592186754645 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754708 1043 #edb/ref 17592186754691 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754708 1043 #edb/ref 17592186754824 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754708 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045461 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754708 1045 "MTH 255 — R-6" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754708 1046 #edb/ref 17592186754448 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754708 1047 #inst "2026-11-06T07:59:00.000Z" 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754708 1048 #edb/ref 17592186405204 13194139546561 17592186502323 true] [17592186754708 1053 #uuid "a8dff835-73e2-561d-b925-4fba56cbab33" 1